msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"A factorial design is an experimental setup used to study the effects of "
"multiple factors by varying them simultaneously. Each factor is tested at "
"different levels and in different combinations with other factors. This "
"design allows for the examination of both the main effects of each factor "
"and the interactions between factors."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"A response surface design is an experimental framework used to optimize and "
"understand the relationships between several explanatory variables and one "
"or more response variables. Besides main effects and interactions, it allows "
"to estimate squared terms, which describe the curvature of the response. "
"This gives a detailed map of the response landscape, which helps to find "
"optimal conditions."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"The measured outcome variables of the process under investigation. Each "
"response is analysed separately."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
