msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"How the sum of squares of each term in the ANOVA table is calculated. The "
"types differ in which other terms a term is adjusted for. In balanced "
"designs with orthogonal (coded) terms, such as complete two-level factorial "
"designs, all types give the same result. In unbalanced designs, e.g. with "
"missing runs, covariates or squared terms, they can differ. The Model, Error "
"and Total rows are the same for all types. See the description of the ANOVA "
"table below."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Sequential sums of squares: each term is adjusted only for the terms entered "
"before it, so the results depend on the order of the terms. The term rows "
"add up to the Model row."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Each term is adjusted for all other terms, except for higher-order terms "
"that contain it. For example, A is adjusted for B, but not for A✻B."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Each term is adjusted for all other terms in the model, i.e. it measures "
"what the term adds when it is entered last. Results for lower-order terms "
"depend on how the factors are coded. Not available when some coefficients "
"are aliased."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Calculate the ANOVA table from the factors in coded units (-1 to 1), so that "
"squared terms are calculated from coded values. Only has an effect when the "
"results are not displayed in coded units. It can change the type II and III "
"sums of squares of the linear terms."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeFactorial|"
msgid ""
"A factorial design is an experimental setup used to study the effects of "
"multiple factors by varying them simultaneously. Each factor is tested at "
"different levels and in different combinations with other factors. This "
"design allows for the examination of both the main effects of each factor "
"and the interactions between factors. It provides a systematic approach to "
"understanding how different variables influence the outcome."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeFactorial|"
msgid "Set the total number of factors in the design."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeFactorial|"
msgid ""
"Set the maximum number of levels for the factors in the design. Only "
"applicable for general full factorial designs, else factors always have two "
"levels. If a factor has fewer levels than the maximum number of levels in "
"the design, leave the remaining level cells empty or add a space."
msgstr ""

